{
  "description": "Interactive Bayes' theorem engine — priors/likelihoods sliders drive a population-grid visualization (true/false positive/negative cells) and a computed posterior via Bayes' rule; a Run Evidence Trial button draws a random individual and accumulates an empirical posterior against the analytic one, on a math-canvas. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
